{"key": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/search?hitsPerPage=20&query=arxiv.org%2Fabs%2F1706.03762&tags=story", "fetched_at": 1786326212.43352, "meta": {"url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/search", "params": {"query": "arxiv.org/abs/1706.03762", "tags": "story", "hitsPerPage": 20}, "kind": "json"}, "payload": {"status": 200, "body": {"exhaustive": {"nbHits": false, "typo": false}, "exhaustiveNbHits": false, "exhaustiveTypo": false, "hits": [{"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "evanhu_"}, "story_text": {"fullyHighlighted": false, "matchLevel": "full", "matchedWords": ["arxiv", ".", "org", "abs", "1706", ".", "03762"], "value": "Hello HN, Talk2Arxiv is a small open-source RAG application I've been building for a few weeks. To use it just prepend any <em>arxiv.org</em> link with 'talk2' to load the paper into a responsive RAG chat application (e.g. www.<em>arxiv.org</em>/<em>abs</em>/<em>1706.03762</em> -&gt; www.talk2arxiv.org/<em>abs</em>/<em>1706.03762</em>).<p>All implementation details are in the GitHub. Currently, because I've opted to extract text from the PDF of the paper rather than reading the LaTeX source code (since I wanted to build a more generic PDF RAG in the process), it struggles with symbolic text / mathematics, and sometimes fails to retrieve the correct context. I appreciate any feedback, and hope people find it useful!<p>Currently, the backend PDF processing server is only single-threaded so if embedding takes a while please be patient!"}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Show HN: Talk to any ArXiv paper just by changing the URL"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://github.com/evanhu1/talk2arxiv"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_evanhu_", "story_38717114", "show_hn"], "author": "evanhu_", "children": [38717177, 38717286, 38717370, 38717371, 38717390, 38717454, 38717464, 38717475, 38717665, 38717755, 38717967, 38718720, 38718898, 38719112, 38719503, 38725518, 38767324], "created_at": "2023-12-21T04:48:20Z", "created_at_i": 1703134100, "num_comments": 73, "objectID": "38717114", "points": 194, "story_id": 38717114, "story_text": "Hello HN, Talk2Arxiv is a small open-source RAG application I&#x27;ve been building for a few weeks. To use it just prepend any arxiv.org link with &#x27;talk2&#x27; to load the paper into a responsive RAG chat application (e.g. www.arxiv.org&#x2F;abs&#x2F;1706.03762 -&gt; www.talk2arxiv.org&#x2F;abs&#x2F;1706.03762).<p>All implementation details are in the GitHub. Currently, because I&#x27;ve opted to extract text from the PDF of the paper rather than reading the LaTeX source code (since I wanted to build a more generic PDF RAG in the process), it struggles with symbolic text &#x2F; mathematics, and sometimes fails to retrieve the correct context. I appreciate any feedback, and hope people find it useful!<p>Currently, the backend PDF processing server is only single-threaded so if embedding takes a while please be patient!", "title": "Show HN: Talk to any ArXiv paper just by changing the URL", "updated_at": "2024-09-20T15:56:55Z", "url": "https://github.com/evanhu1/talk2arxiv"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "jerpint"}, "story_text": {"fullyHighlighted": false, "matchLevel": "full", "matchedWords": ["arxiv", ".", "org", "abs", "1706", ".", "03762"], "value": "Just change <em>arxiv.org</em> to arxiv-txt.org in the URL to get the paper info in markdown<p>Example:<p>Original URL:\n<a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.03762\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://<em>arxiv.org</em>/<em>abs</em>/<em>1706.03762</em></a><p>Change to:\n<a href=\"https://arxiv-txt.org/abs/1706.03762\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://arxiv-txt.org/<em>abs</em>/<em>1706.03762</em></a><p>To fetch the raw text directly, use <a href=\"https://arxiv-txt.org/raw/abs/1706.03762\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://arxiv-txt.org/raw/<em>abs</em>/<em>1706.03762</em></a>, this will be particularly useful for APIs and agents"}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Show HN: ArXiv-txt, LLM-friendly ArXiv papers"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://www.arxiv-txt.org/"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_jerpint", "story_43111112", "show_hn"], "author": "jerpint", "children": [43112989, 43115191, 43115227, 43116259, 43132536, 43187585], "created_at": "2025-02-20T04:23:54Z", "created_at_i": 1740025434, "num_comments": 11, "objectID": "43111112", "points": 22, "story_id": 43111112, "story_text": "Just change arxiv.org to arxiv-txt.org in the URL to get the paper info in markdown<p>Example:<p>Original URL:\n<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;arxiv.org&#x2F;abs&#x2F;1706.03762\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;arxiv.org&#x2F;abs&#x2F;1706.03762</a><p>Change to:\n<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;arxiv-txt.org&#x2F;abs&#x2F;1706.03762\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;arxiv-txt.org&#x2F;abs&#x2F;1706.03762</a><p>To fetch the raw text directly, use <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;arxiv-txt.org&#x2F;raw&#x2F;abs&#x2F;1706.03762\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;arxiv-txt.org&#x2F;raw&#x2F;abs&#x2F;1706.03762</a>, this will be particularly useful for APIs and agents", "title": "Show HN: ArXiv-txt, LLM-friendly ArXiv papers", "updated_at": "2025-03-01T00:54:33Z", "url": "https://www.arxiv-txt.org/"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "melvinmelih"}, "story_text": {"fullyHighlighted": false, "matchLevel": "full", "matchedWords": ["arxiv", ".", "org", "abs", "1706", ".", "03762"], "value": "I created this tool over the weekend because, as someone interested in AI and technology, I find many research papers on arXiv fascinating but often incredibly dense and difficult to understand due to the heavy jargon and technical language. I wanted to make these complex topics more accessible to laypeople like myself by converting the topics described in these papers into full-length books that break down key concepts, making cutting-edge research easier to grasp. You can think of it as generating prerequisite reading materials before being able to read the actual paper.<p>Here are some noteworthy arXiv papers you can test this with:<p>- Attention is All You Need: <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.03762\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://<em>arxiv.org</em>/<em>abs</em>/<em>1706.03762</em></a><p>- BERT: Pre-training of Deep Bidirectional Transformers for Language Understanding: <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.04805\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://<em>arxiv.org</em>/<em>abs</em>/1810.04805</a><p>- GPT-3: Language Models are Few-Shot Learners: <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.14165\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://<em>arxiv.org</em>/<em>abs</em>/2005.14165</a><p>- Deep Residual Learning for Image Recognition (ResNet): <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.03385\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://<em>arxiv.org</em>/<em>abs</em>/1512.03385</a><p>The tool leverages GPT-4o, Perplexity, and Instructor to analyze and break down the complex concepts within these papers. Keep in mind, it's not built for heavy traffic (current capacity is about 50 books per hour) so if things get busy, it may take a bit longer, but the book will arrive via email eventually!"}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Show HN: Turn Any ArXiv Paper into a 200-Page Prerequisite Reading Book"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://instabooks.ai/pages/arxiv-books"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_melvinmelih", "story_41491707", "show_hn"], "author": "melvinmelih", "children": [41492221, 41492957], "created_at": "2024-09-09T18:23:51Z", "created_at_i": 1725906231, "num_comments": 3, "objectID": "41491707", "points": 6, "story_id": 41491707, "story_text": "I created this tool over the weekend because, as someone interested in AI and technology, I find many research papers on arXiv fascinating but often incredibly dense and difficult to understand due to the heavy jargon and technical language. I wanted to make these complex topics more accessible to laypeople like myself by converting the topics described in these papers into full-length books that break down key concepts, making cutting-edge research easier to grasp. You can think of it as generating prerequisite reading materials before being able to read the actual paper.<p>Here are some noteworthy arXiv papers you can test this with:<p>- Attention is All You Need: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;arxiv.org&#x2F;abs&#x2F;1706.03762\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;arxiv.org&#x2F;abs&#x2F;1706.03762</a><p>- BERT: Pre-training of Deep Bidirectional Transformers for Language Understanding: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;arxiv.org&#x2F;abs&#x2F;1810.04805\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;arxiv.org&#x2F;abs&#x2F;1810.04805</a><p>- GPT-3: Language Models are Few-Shot Learners: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;arxiv.org&#x2F;abs&#x2F;2005.14165\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;arxiv.org&#x2F;abs&#x2F;2005.14165</a><p>- Deep Residual Learning for Image Recognition (ResNet): <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;arxiv.org&#x2F;abs&#x2F;1512.03385\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;arxiv.org&#x2F;abs&#x2F;1512.03385</a><p>The tool leverages GPT-4o, Perplexity, and Instructor to analyze and break down the complex concepts within these papers. Keep in mind, it&#x27;s not built for heavy traffic (current capacity is about 50 books per hour) so if things get busy, it may take a bit longer, but the book will arrive via email eventually!", "title": "Show HN: Turn Any ArXiv Paper into a 200-Page Prerequisite Reading Book", "updated_at": "2025-09-03T07:27:14Z", "url": "https://instabooks.ai/pages/arxiv-books"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "baymax05"}, "story_text": {"fullyHighlighted": false, "matchLevel": "full", "matchedWords": ["arxiv", ".", "org", "abs", "1706", ".", "03762"], "value": "Attention Is All You Need paper got an updated submission with this red note<p>&quot;Provided proper attribution is provided, Google hereby grants permission to reproduce the tables and figures in this paper solely for use in journalistic or scholarly works.&quot;\nhttps://<em>arxiv.org</em>/<em>abs</em>/<em>1706.03762</em>v7"}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Only journalistic or scholarly works are permitted for Attention paper"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_baymax05", "story_37614690", "ask_hn"], "author": "baymax05", "created_at": "2023-09-22T17:13:06Z", "created_at_i": 1695402786, "num_comments": 0, "objectID": "37614690", "points": 1, "story_id": 37614690, "story_text": "Attention Is All You Need paper got an updated submission with this red note<p>&quot;Provided proper attribution is provided, Google hereby grants permission to reproduce the tables and figures in this paper solely for use in journalistic or scholarly works.&quot;\nhttps:&#x2F;&#x2F;arxiv.org&#x2F;abs&#x2F;1706.03762v7", "title": "Only journalistic or scholarly works are permitted for Attention paper", "updated_at": "2024-09-20T15:09:29Z"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "nadermx"}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "The paper that made ChatGPT possible"}, "url": {"fullyHighlighted": false, "matchLevel": "full", "matchedWords": ["arxiv", ".", "org", "abs", "1706", ".", "03762"], "value": "https://<em>arxiv.org</em>/<em>abs</em>/<em>1706.03762</em>"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_nadermx", "story_34649113"], "author": "nadermx", "children": [34651201, 34651613, 34651673, 34651847, 34651900, 34652125, 34652295, 34652302, 34652927, 34653324, 34653467, 34653711, 34653723, 34654182, 34654536, 34654720, 34655718, 34657183, 34658335], "created_at": "2023-02-03T23:07:16Z", "created_at_i": 1675465636, "num_comments": 55, "objectID": "34649113", "points": 173, "story_id": 34649113, "title": "The paper that made ChatGPT possible", "updat